# Milestone: M3
# Covers: exception regressions: uninitialized var += in catch; asString exception
#         in asTopLevelPrintable; 1:1 non-tag colon error; scheduler stuck on
#         concurrent throw + freeze scenario.
# defer-to: M4 (requires e.isA(Float) method guard, 'at (e?)' reactive watcher, freeze)
#
# Reason:
#   Several cases in this fixture require M4+: 'catch(var e if e.isA(Float))' uses
#   isA() method dispatch (M4); 'class X { function asString() { 0/0 } }' uses
#   class definition (M4); the scheduler-stuck regression case uses ',' and 't.freeze'
#   method (M5).  The uninitialized-var-in-catch pattern (var test; test += 3) and
#   bare-throw from inside a catch block could partially work at M3 but the fixture
#   as a whole cannot pass until M4+ is available.
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at M4 with exception type hierarchy and class definition):
# # var test; try { test += 3 } catch { test = 1; test += 3 };
# # [00000001] 4
